  <article class="article">
    <a class="backlink" href="/en/">← Back to home</a>
    <h1>Privacy Notice</h1>
    <p class="lead">This notice describes how personal data is processed in connection with the use of the website of Czudar DHH Ügyvédi Iroda (drczudar.hu), in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) and Hungarian Act CXII of 2011 on Informational Self-Determination and Freedom of Information (the Info Act).</p>
    <div class="body">

      <h2>1. The controller and contact details</h2>
      <p>The data controller:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Name:</strong> Czudar DHH Ügyvédi Iroda <em>(⚠️ to be verified: the firm’s exact registered name should be confirmed by the attorney — the mandatory bar text also uses the name “Czudar Ügyvédi Iroda”)</em></li>
        <li><strong>Registered seat:</strong> 1054 Budapest, Szemere u. 23. I/1., Hungary</li>
        <li><strong>Branch office:</strong> 2660 Balassagyarmat, Rákóczi fejedelem út 13., Hungary</li>
        <li><strong>E-mail:</strong> info@drczudar.hu</li>
        <li><strong>Phone:</strong> +36 1 577 9191</li>
        <li><strong>Bar registration:</strong> Budapest Bar Association, registration no. 5160</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The firm is not required to appoint a data protection officer under Article 37 GDPR; data-protection enquiries may be addressed to the controller using the contact details above. <em>(⚠️ to be verified: whether a data protection officer must be appointed, and its contact details.)</em></p>

      <h2>2. Data processed in connection with the website</h2>

      <h3>2.1 Contact by e-mail and telephone</h3>
      <p>If you contact us using the e-mail address or telephone number shown on the website, we process the data you provide: your name, e-mail address, telephone number and the content of your enquiry. We process this data to respond to your enquiry and to prepare any potential engagement.</p>

      <h3>2.2 Online appointment booking (Google Calendar)</h3>
      <p>The online appointment booking available through the website operates via Google Calendar. The data provided for the booking (e.g. name, e-mail address, the requested time and the subject of the enquiry) is recorded in Google’s system. In this respect <strong>Google acts as a processor</strong>, handling the booking data on behalf of and on the instructions of the controller.</p>

      <h3>2.3 Embedded Google Maps</h3>
      <p>The website may display the firm’s location using an <strong>embedded Google Map (Google Maps)</strong>. When the map loads, <strong>Google may set cookies and process technical data (e.g. IP address, device and browser information)</strong> for its own services. This constitutes Google’s own processing, governed by Google’s privacy policy. <em>(⚠️ to be verified: whether the embedded map is actually active on the site, and in what configuration.)</em></p>

      <h3>2.4 Server and hosting logs</h3>
      <p>The website is hosted by <strong>GitHub (GitHub Pages)</strong>. The website consists of static pages; on the hosting side the provider may, as is customary, process technical logs (e.g. IP address, time of the request, page requested, browser identifier) for the provision and security of the service. <em>(⚠️ to be verified: the scope and retention of the log data actually processed by GitHub Pages.)</em></p>

      <h3>2.5 Social-media links</h3>
      <p>The website may contain links to external social-media providers. By clicking these links you are taken to the external provider’s site, whose processing is the responsibility of that provider and is governed by that provider’s own privacy policy.</p>

      <h2>3. Purposes and legal bases of processing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Contact, responding to enquiries, preparing an engagement</strong> — legal basis: steps taken prior to entering into a contract, or performance of a contract (Article 6(1)(b) GDPR).</li>
        <li><strong>Handling online appointment bookings</strong> — legal basis: measures taken at your request prior to entering into a contract (Article 6(1)(b) GDPR).</li>
        <li><strong>Operation and security of the website, display of the embedded map, and technical/statistical logging</strong> — legal basis: the controller’s legitimate interest (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).</li>
        <li><strong>Cookies that are not strictly necessary, set by the embedded Google services</strong> — legal basis: your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR). <em>(⚠️ to be verified: whether a consent-management tool (cookie banner) is required for the embedded services.)</em></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Retention periods</h2>
      <p>We process personal data only for as long as necessary to achieve the purposes above, and for the retention periods prescribed by law. Enquiries are retained for the time needed to respond to them and — where an engagement is established — to comply with the statutory obligations relating to that engagement. <em>(⚠️ to be verified: the specific retention periods — e.g. for enquiries, bookings, logs — should be confirmed by the attorney; this notice deliberately states no specific months/years.)</em></p>

      <h2>5. Processors and data transfers</h2>
      <p>The controller uses the following processors:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google</strong> (online appointment booking via Google Calendar; embedded Google Maps). Certain Google services may involve transfers outside the European Economic Area, governed by the appropriate safeguards provided by Google (e.g. a European Commission adequacy decision or standard contractual clauses).</li>
        <li><strong>GitHub</strong> (hosting of the website, GitHub Pages).</li>
      </ul>
      <p><em>(⚠️ to be verified: the exact set of processors, the data-processing agreements concluded with them, and the fact of and specific safeguards for any transfer outside the EEA.)</em></p>
      <p><strong>International transfers in connection with the DHH network / China desk:</strong> where the nature of an engagement so requires, data may be transferred within the framework of network cooperation. <em>(⚠️ to be verified: whether this actually occurs within the scope of website-related processing; if so, it may only be stated with the appropriate safeguards under Chapter V GDPR — otherwise this paragraph should be deleted.)</em></p>

      <h2>6. Your rights as a data subject</h2>
      <p>In connection with the processing you may exercise the following rights:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access to your personal data;</li>
        <li>rectification (correction of inaccurate data, completion of incomplete data);</li>
        <li>erasure (the “right to be forgotten”);</li>
        <li>restriction of processing;</li>
        <li>objection to processing based on legitimate interest;</li>
        <li>data portability;</li>
        <li>where processing is based on consent, withdrawal of consent at any time (this does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before withdrawal).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You may submit a request to exercise your rights using the contact details set out in section 1. We will provide information in response without undue delay. The exercise of these rights may be limited by the rules on legal professional privilege and by statutory retention obligations (see section 8).</p>

      <h2>7. Remedies</h2>
      <p>If you consider that the processing infringes your rights, you may lodge a complaint with the supervisory authority:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Hungarian National Authority for Data Protection and Freedom of Information (NAIH)</strong>, Budapest.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You are also entitled to seek a judicial remedy. Proceedings may — at your choice — be brought before the tribunal of your place of residence or place of stay.</p>

      <h2>8. Legal professional privilege</h2>
      <p>Client data processed in connection with engagements is governed by legal professional privilege (attorney–client confidentiality) and by Act LXXVIII of 2017 on the Activities of Attorneys-at-Law. The protection of privileged information and the professional and legal liability rest solely with the acting attorney. In respect of privileged data, data-subject rights — in particular access and erasure — may be exercised only within the limits of the confidentiality obligation and the statutory retention requirements.</p>

      <h2>9. Cookie information</h2>
      <p>The website is built from static pages and <strong>does not itself set any cookies</strong> on your device. However, the embedded Google services (Google Maps and the Google booking interface) <strong>may set cookies and process technical data</strong> when they load. These are governed by Google’s own privacy and cookie policies. <em>(⚠️ to be verified: the scope and lifetime of the cookies actually set, and whether a consent-management solution is required.)</em></p>

    </div>
